{%- comment -%}
  bbc-chapter-list — quiet "on this page" anchor list for long pages (2026-07-24).
  GOV.UK-pattern wayfinding: plain anchor links, NOT sticky — the 8-site impact-page
  layout tour found zero sticky rails in the genre; anchors passed the ≥3-site
  threshold (charity:water #donate · Switchback Reshape #action · GOV.UK long pages).
  Usage: {% render 'bbc-chapter-list', chapters: 'the ask~#book-a-call|the proof~#proof', label: 'on this page' %}
  Pairs split on '|', label/anchor on '~' (commas in labels stay safe — press-canon lesson).
  No JS, no sticky, no active state. Targets need scroll-margin-top (universal §9).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if chapters != blank -%}
<nav class="bbc-chapters" aria-label="On this page">
  {%- if label != blank -%}<span class="bbc-chapters__label">{{ label }}</span>{%- endif -%}
  <ul class="bbc-chapters__list" role="list">
    {%- assign _pairs = chapters | split: '|' -%}
    {%- for pair in _pairs -%}
      {%- assign _p = pair | split: '~' -%}
      {%- if _p[1] != blank -%}
      <li><a href="{{ _p[1] | strip }}">{{ _p[0] | strip }}</a></li>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
</nav>
{%- endif -%}
